  "solution": "<p>For a non-negative integer variable, E[N] = Σ<sub>k≥0</sub> P(N &gt; k). The event N &gt; k says the first k rolls are distinct, so P(N &gt; k) = 6!/((6−k)!·6<sup>k</sup>).</p><p>k = 0..6: 1, 1, 5/6, 5/9, 5/18, 5/54, 5/324 (and 0 for k ≥ 7, since a 7th roll must repeat).</p><p>Sum = (324 + 324 + 270 + 180 + 90 + 30 + 5)/324 = 1223/324 ≈ 3.775.</p><p>Trap: summing P(N = k) by hand is slower and error-prone; the tail-sum formula does it in one line.</p><p><b>Answer: 1223/324 ≈ 3.775.</b></p>",
