  "solution": "<p>With k bulbs working, the time to the next failure is the minimum of k exponentials: exponential with mean 1000/k. By memorylessness the survivors are as good as new, so the gaps are independent.</p><p>E[max] = 1000(1/4 + 1/3 + 1/2 + 1) = 1000·25/12 ≈ 2083.3 hours.</p><p>Trap: answering 4000 (adding the means) or 1000 (one mean). The maximum of n exponentials grows only like log n.</p><p><b>Answer: 6250/3 ≈ 2083.3 hours.</b></p>",
