  "solution": "<p>For b ≤ 100, the owner accepts with probability b/100, and given acceptance V ~ U(0, b).</p><p>Conditional profit = 1.8·(b/2) + 10 − b = 10 − 0.1b.</p><p>Expected profit π(b) = (b/100)(10 − 0.1b) = 0.1b − 0.001b². π′(b) = 0.1 − 0.002b = 0 ⇒ b = 50, π = 5 − 2.5 = 2.5.</p><p>Trap: computing with the unconditional mean E[V] = 50 (value 1.8·50 + 10 = 100 &gt; any bid) makes every bid look good. Acceptance tells you V is low: the winner's curse. Without the +10 synergy the best bid would be 0.</p><p><b>Answer: bid 50, expected profit 2.5.</b></p>",
