  "solution": "<p>The situation repeats after each rejection, so the value V of the game is constant and you accept exactly when X ≥ V. It satisfies V = −c + E[max(X, V)], i.e. c = E[(X − V)<sup>+</sup>] = (1 − V)²/2.</p><p>With c = 0.005: (1 − V)² = 0.01 ⇒ V = 0.9.</p><p>Each offer clears the threshold with probability 0.1, so the number of offers is geometric with mean 10. Check: expected payoff = E[X | X ≥ 0.9] − 10c = 0.95 − 0.05 = 0.9 = V ✓.</p><p>Trap: setting the threshold to E[X] = 0.5, or forgetting that the cost is paid on every offer seen.</p><p><b>Answer: 0.9, 10.</b></p>",
