  "solution": "<p>Let A<sub>i</sub> be the set of permutations containing 'i, i+1' consecutively (i = 1..7). Forcing any k of these glues numbers into blocks, leaving 8 − k units, which can be arranged in (8 − k)! ways (the patterns always combine consistently into increasing runs).</p><p>Count = Σ<sub>k=0..7</sub> (−1)<sup>k</sup> C(7, k)(8 − k)! = 40320 − 35280 + 15120 − 4200 + 840 − 126 + 14 − 1 = 16687.</p><p>Trap: thinking the overlapping patterns (like 12 and 23) conflict. They are compatible and form the block 123.</p><p><b>Answer: 16687.</b></p>",
