  "prompt": "<p>Three players each get a red or blue hat, independently and uniformly at random. Each sees the other two hats but not their own. Without communicating, they simultaneously either guess their own colour or pass. The team wins if at least one player guesses and nobody guesses wrong. They may agree on a strategy beforehand. What is the highest possible winning probability?</p><p>Give a fraction or decimal.</p>",
