  "solution": "<p>g(f) = 0.36 ln(1 + 2f) + 0.48 ln 1 + 0.16 ln(1 − 2f).</p><p>g′ = 0: 0.72/(1 + 2f) = 0.32/(1 − 2f) ⇒ 0.72 − 1.44f = 0.32 + 0.64f ⇒ f = 0.4/2.08 = 5/26 ≈ 0.1923.</p><p>That is slightly less than the single-bet Kelly 0.2 each: the bets are resolved simultaneously, so you can't compound between them and the downside 1 − 2f is harsher.</p><p><b>Answer: 5/26 ≈ 0.192.</b></p>",
