  "solution": "<p>At leverage c·μ/σ²: drift ν = (c − c²/2)μ²/σ², variance s² = c²μ²/σ², so θ = 2ν/s² = (2 − c)/c = 3 for c = ½.</p><p>W<sup>−3</sup> is then a martingale: p·2<sup>−3</sup> + (1 − p)·2<sup>3</sup> = 1 ⇒ 8 − (63/8)p = 1 ⇒ p = 56/63 = 8/9.</p><p>Halving the bet raises the doubling-first probability from 2/3 to 8/9 while still keeping 75% of the growth rate.</p><p><b>Answer: 8/9 ≈ 0.889.</b></p>",
