  "solution": "<p>Posterior: P(A | H) = (0.5·0.7)/(0.5·0.7 + 0.5·0.4) = 0.35/0.55 = 7/11.</p><p>Predictive P(heads next) = (7/11)(0.7) + (4/11)(0.4) = 6.5/11 = 13/22.</p><p>The next bet's outcome is binary, so maximising E[ln W] only needs this predictive probability: f = 2p − 1 = 26/22 − 1 = 2/11 ≈ 0.182 (before the first flip it was 2(0.55) − 1 = 0.10).</p><p><b>Answer: 2/11.</b></p>",
