  "solution": "<p>λ<sub>a</sub>/λ<sub>b</sub> = e<sup>−k(0.5 − m)</sup>/e<sup>−k(0.5 + m)</sup> = e<sup>2km</sup>. With competing Poisson flows, P(next fill is at ask) = λ<sub>a</sub>/(λ<sub>a</sub> + λ<sub>b</sub>) = 0.8 ⇔ ratio 4.</p><p>e<sup>3m</sup> = 4 ⇒ m = ln 4 / 3 ≈ 0.462. The width does not matter, only the shift.</p><p><b>Answer: ≈ 0.462.</b></p>",
