  "prompt": "<p>A, B and C fight a truel, shooting in the order A, B, C, A, B, C, … (skipping anyone hit). A hits with probability 1/3, B with 2/3, C never misses. B and C always aim at the most accurate opponent still standing; once two remain they shoot at each other. On his first turn A may aim at B, aim at C, or deliberately miss; afterwards he shoots at whoever is left. With A's best first-turn choice, what is A's probability of survival?</p><p>Give a fraction or decimal.</p>",
