  "style": [
   "math-test",
   "trading-desk"
  ],
  "prompt": "<p>Workers are high-productivity (worth 2 to employers) or low (worth 1). A worker chooses an education level e ≥ 0 that adds no productivity but costs e for a high type and 2e for a low type. Employers pay a wage equal to expected productivity given e. In a separating equilibrium high types choose e* and low types choose 0 (and get wage 1). For which range of e* is this an equilibrium? (Treat an indifferent worker as following the equilibrium.)</p><p>Answer as two numbers separated by a comma: lowest e*, highest e*.</p>",
